This gives me a Camera Operation Table containing in each cell (that is for each day and each station), the total number of sessions for which that station was operating, rather then the number of active cameras on that day. If for example there are 2 sessions,

·         a station with 1 camera would result in the value 2 in each cell (if the camera was active on that day)

·         a station with 2 cameras would result in the value 4 if both cameras were active in both sessions

·         a station with 2 cameras would result in the value 3 if one of the cameras was active only for one session

When I try camerasIndependent = TRUE, I obtain NAs, 1s and 0s, which is more ‘accurate’ but I loose the information on the number of active cameras per day (If a station has 3 active cameras during an occasion of 6 days, I would like the usage for that occasion to be 18).

I continued with this last Camera Operation Table (with camerasIndependent = TRUE, and therefore only 1s and 0s in the resulting table), and ran the spatialDetectionHistory function on my Record Individual Table (which does not contain Sessioncol), as followed:

